# Lesson 3.5 example: inspect record fields and nested records

# The invoice field is itself a record, so this example has nested data.
invoice equals record with 1200 as amount and "pending" as status
review_packet equals record with invoice as invoice and "Ada" as reviewer

# Keys, values, and entries expose a record in three different shapes.
packet_keys equals keys of review_packet
packet_values equals values of review_packet
packet_entries equals entries of review_packet

# Read through nested records from right to left: invoice of review_packet, then amount of invoice.
review_amount equals amount of invoice of review_packet

Print packet_keys
Print review_amount

# Entries are records with key and value fields.
For each entry in packet_entries:
  Print key of entry
